# The interactive shell has one inherently large dispatch function: the agent-mode
# event loop (runAgentModeFlow), a single coroutine that owns the agent worker,
# screen, components, and a long message/event switch (~2200 lines, ~990
# statements vs. the 800 threshold). Bringing it under the limit requires
# extracting the per-event dispatch — including a `co_return` that exits agent mode
# and ~20 mutated/read loop locals — behind a context struct + an exit-signal
# protocol. That is a sizable, regression-prone refactor of an interactive path
# with no unit-test seam, so it is tracked separately rather than rushed.
#
# The natural extraction seam is now in place: the four inline prompts
# (askUser / permission / sessionPicker / planApproval) are each driven through
# `QuestionComponent::step()` (ModalComponent contract), so they are cohesive units
# ready to move into helpers when the split is done.
#
# Until then, disable only the function-size check for this directory; all other
# checks are inherited from the repo root.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: '-readability-function-size'
